Director Independence

The Nasdaq listing standards require that a majority of our board of directors be independent. An “independent director” is defined generally as a person who, in the opinion of the company’s board of directors, has no material relationship with the listed company (either directly or as a partner, shareholder or officer of an organization that has a relationship with the company). We have three “independent directors” as defined in the Nasdaq listing standards and applicable SEC rules. Our board has determined that each of Mr. Ashley Bancroft, Mr. Nathan Pau and Ms. Tracy Hui Yin Choi are independent directors under applicable SEC and Nasdaq rules. Our independent directors will have meetings at which only independent directors are present.
